  "name": "Move route",
  "kind": "route",
  "responsibility": "Moves a whole board into another repository's vault under the write's admission, tells each vault's panes and takes the board's panes along; says beforehand what a move would rewrite",
  "description": "TASK-472.15, ADR 0051: semantic move. move.to names the target vault, read as strictly as the vault of the call. The source vault's change feed says the board moved and where to. A move that stopped part way announces what it wrote, moves no pane, and answers MOVE_STOPPED. TASK-472.16: movePreviewRoute answers GET move-preview, holding and writing nothing, so it takes no lease and no claim; it can be out of date when the move runs, and the version it answers is the version the move states. A board name that cannot be used is refused as every write refuses it (BAD_BOARD_NAME, through usableBoard), and any other refusal is answered in the move's own words and codes.",
